\[
\begin{array}{c|c|c}
\multicolumn{1}{c}{}
& \multicolumn{1}{c}{\textbf{Passes Engineering Mechanics Test}} & \multicolumn{1}{c}{\textbf{Does Not Pass Engineering Mechanics Test}} \\
\cline{2-3}
\text{Passes Advanced Graphic Editing Test} & 68 & 24 \\
\text{Does Not Pass Advanced Graphic Editing Test} & 85 & 18 \\
\end{array}
\]

Based on these results, what is the expected number of users who will pass both tests, also fitting in an online coding proficiency test, where 70\% of those who pass only one of the original two tests pass?
